{"id": "sdqa0112", "pool": "sdqa", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3492556793, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "9d39a2003e15ffbac1b46fe5b0a53c242ef024ed6b8b1e37a92e22d426213d95", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "When was the Epic of Gilgamesh discovered?", "input_path": "/data/sdqa_audio/sdqa0112.wav", "input_sha256": "05bd68ecbbdb974b8fb7a36cba81377d668b5c56daac3c3b6a7f3f9e1fb11d0b", "input_samples": 82256, "input_s": 5.141, "n_real_chunks": 6, "score": 0.5339, "act": 0.9998, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "The Epic of Gilgamesh was rediscovered in modern times in 1853, when clay tablets containing the story were excavated by Hormuzd Rassam at the ruins of Nineveh, in the library of the Assyrian king Ashurbanipal. It became widely recognized after George Smith translated parts of it in 1872.", "expert_answer": "The **Epic of Gilgamesh** was rediscovered in modern times in **1853**, when clay tablets containing the story were excavated by **Hormuzd Rassam** at the ruins of **Nineveh**, in the library of the Assyrian king **Ashurbanipal**.\n\nIt became widely recognized after **George Smith** translated parts of it in **1872**.", "transcript": "When was the Epic of Gilgamesh discovered?\n", "asr_s": 0.71, "expert_s": 3.71, "expert_input_samples": 80000, "expert_input_s": 5.0, "expert_input_sha256": "8a6b5c8d06b13ab8c3a2c2173e2e16e9ceefbf5438e230a99912f8e0f2207096", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 3.803, "relay_synth_ms": 10877, "onset_chunk": 4, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0112_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "571e4727a138cc3a890d90ff615e10d3e210b01b1faa203af51be8e7cc0fc482", "sr": 24